import ExponentialIdentities.TwoBaseIntegerExponent.FiniteCheck8192

namespace LeanProofs.TwoBaseIntegerExponent

open Set

/-!
This file extends the exact finite verification from `8192` to `16384`: any real exponent with
`2 ^ x` and `3 ^ x` both integral and `2 ^ x < 16384` is an integer, so a nonintegral solution
must satisfy `x ≥ 14`.

The architecture is that of `FiniteCheck8192`.  For each nonpower-of-two `m` with
`8192 ≤ m < 16384` the table records `a = ⌊m ^ (log 3 / log 2)⌋` and a tier selecting a pair of
rational enclosures of `log 3 / log 2`; the lower enclosures are continued-fraction
convergents and semiconvergents, the upper enclosures are convergents and semiconvergents.  The two integer power comparisons `a ^ Lq < m ^ Lp` and
`m ^ Up < (a + 1) ^ Uq`, together with the tier base enclosures `2 ^ Lp < 3 ^ Lq` and
`3 ^ Uq < 2 ^ Up`, trap `m ^ (log 3 / log 2)` strictly between consecutive integers.  The
table was generated with `mpmath` and every row re-verified with exact Python big-integer
arithmetic before being replayed by the kernel through `decide`.
-/

set_option maxRecDepth 200000 in
